{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The mitigation is submitted and the endpoint returned 200.\n\n**Root cause:** The `search` deployment could not create any pods. The namespace has a `memory-limit-quota` (1Gi), and the search container had no memory request or limit, so every ReplicaSet create was rejected with \"must specify memory\". Search was down, which degraded requests that depend on it.\n\n**Fix:** Added `requests.memory: 128Mi` and `limits.memory: 256Mi` to the `hotel-reserv-search` container in the `search` deployment with `kubectl patch`. The rollout completed, and the pod is Running and registered with Consul. The quota now shows 128Mi of 1Gi used.\n\n**Other observations:**\n- The `profile` pod restarted once at startup (exit code 2). Its logs show it started cleanly after that, so I didn't change it.\n- Other deployments still have no memory requests. They're running now, but any future pod recreation in this namespace will hit the same quota rejection. Setting memory requests on all deployments would prevent that."}}
